  "transcript": [
    {
      "approx_t": 0.0,
      "text": "The lips can make or break a face."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 0.02,
      "text": "Here are two simple steps with the highest return to naturally improve them."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 0.05,
      "text": "Step one is fixing lip posture, which radically transforms the perceived dimensions of your lips."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 0.1,
      "text": "Half of you are tucking your top lip in without even realizing it, which in turn makes it appear thinner,"
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 0.15,
      "text": "and many of you are curling the outer corners of your lips downwards without realizing."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 0.19,
      "text": "The literature indicates that these changes make the face appear less youthful, less friendly, and less attractive."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 0.25,
      "text": "What you should practice instead is the habit of a gentle pout and the soft smile as a new resting phase"
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 0.29,
      "text": "for a younger, kinder, and more esthetic mouth."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 0.33,
      "text": "The second step is to not just focus on lip size."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 0.35,
      "text": "Thin lips can still be very attractive if they are hydrated and have sufficient red pigment."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 0.4,
      "text": "So one of the oldest tricks is to simply make red- or pink-tinted lip balm a staple of your daily routine."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 0.46,
      "text": "As a man you might think, 'Oh, let me skip the color,'"
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 0.48,
      "text": "but Stephen and McKeegan found red pigment also makes men's lips more attractive too,"
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 0.52,
      "text": "and tinted lip balm is not like lipstick."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 0.55,
      "text": "Realistically, if you pick a mild one, you'll look better and nobody will notice why."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 0.59,
      "text": "There are dozens of small signals like these that shape how your face is perceived,"
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 1.02,
      "text": "and we break down all of them over at Qoves.com."
    }
  ],
